+# ETFS_GUARDRAIL.TO-EG-s-24 -- THE FORCING SEAM, AND WHY IT IS SHAPED THIS WAY.
+#
+# The renderer has carried `--fixture-remove` since EG-s-6 (declared at
+# render_month_end.py:1022, parsed by _parse_fixture_remove at :852, applied at
+# :1030/:1033/:1040/:1047). It drops dates from the loaded series IN MEMORY and
+# touches nothing on S3. This orchestrator never threaded it, so FWD-9's forced
+# class-C condition was unreachable by construction and no seat could drive a
+# refusal -- row W4-S2, which is why EG-s-21 could not be executed as cut.
+#
+# WARN: THIS OVERRIDE IS WORSE-SHAPED THAN A `--month` OVERRIDE AND IS TREATED AS SUCH.
+# CLAUDE.md: an override that lets a scheduled producer run off its own inputs
+# CREATES A NEW REACHABLE STATE on the manual path, and the sign-off covers that
+# state or the override does not land. A `--month` override changes WHICH month is
+# rendered; THIS one makes the monthly report DROP ITS OWN INPUT DATA. A scheduled
+# fire able to reach it would publish a report over data it silently removed. So:
+#
+#   1. THE DEFAULT IS OFF. `_forcing_spec` returns "" for every event that does not
+#      ask for forcing explicitly, and "" appends NOTHING to the render command --
+#      the marker-free command string is bit-for-bit what it was before this change.
+#   2. TWO INDEPENDENT CONDITIONS, NEITHER IN THE SCHEDULED PAYLOAD. The event must
+#      carry BOTH the TEST_MARKER (`test_run`, EG-s-20's own marker) AND
+#      FORCING_KEY. The EventBridge schedule's input is jsonencode({mode = "run"})
+#      (infra/aws/terraform/etfs-reports/orchestrator.tf) and carries neither.
+#   3. THE COUPLING IS THE SAFETY COMPOSITION, NOT CONVENIENCE: because forcing
+#      requires the TEST marker, a run that removes its own input data can NEVER be
+#      a run whose recipients include aj@ -- EG-s-20's filter runs last on exactly
+#      that marker. Data-forcing and Andrew's ~02:5xZ constraint cannot come apart.
+#   4. THE SPEC IS SHELL-BOUND. _render_command interpolates into a single-quoted
+#      `su - ec2-user -c '...'` string handed to SSM, so an unvalidated spec is a
+#      command-injection surface. FORCING_SPEC_RE admits ONLY
+#      `<partner>:<YYYY-MM-DD>[,<YYYY-MM-DD>...]` -- no quote, space, semicolon,
+#      backtick or `$` can survive it. Anything else resolves to "" (OFF) and says so.
+FORCING_KEY = "force_fixture_remove"
+FORCING_SPEC_RE = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,31}:\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}(,\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})*$")
 # The shared critical-surface channel the COO polls every /drive cycle. Every fail-loud alert ALSO
 # goes here so a failed/no-show monthly run is caught structurally (not just by Andrew's email sub).
